---
description: Apply the frozen native Nuxt Vue shadcn-vue UI architecture
globs:
  - "app/**/*.vue"
  - "app/**/*.ts"
  - "app/**/*.css"
  - "nuxt.config.ts"
  - "components.json"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Read the installed UI constitution before planning or changing UI code.
- Build with native Nuxt/Vue SFCs and the checked-in shadcn-vue/Reka
  primitives under `app/components/ui`.
- Product components compose primitives; do not create a second generic
  wrapper design system or clone existing primitives.
- Tailwind is part of shadcn-vue. Use semantic tokens, existing primitive
  styles and typed CVA variants; avoid repeated arbitrary utility class policy.
- Route remote data through typed composables, `DieRepository` and the
  generated `/die/v1` client. Never hand-edit generated DTOs.
- Preserve unknown, partial, unsupported, stale, unauthorized and redacted
  states exactly.
- Do not join sensors, infer canonical identity or calculate product truth in
  the browser.
- Use TanStack Vue Table, Unovis/Vue and Vue Flow only for their frozen,
  bounded roles and provide accessible alternatives.
- Run component, contract, accessibility, authorization-state, typecheck,
  lint, production-build and fixture-reachability gates as applicable.
